\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Acquisition witness}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{evaluation}

\p{A \strong{witness family} is a prespecified measurable assignment
#{q\mapsto W(q)} of accepted evaluation trajectories. Define}

##{
 s_W(\pi)=\mathbb E_{q\sim\mathcal Q_{\mathrm{ev}}}
 \left[\mathbb P^{D,b}_{q,\pi}\{\tau\in W(q)\}\right].
}

\p{For declared thresholds #{0\leq\alpha<\beta\leq1}, the family is an
\strong{acquisition witness} for protocol #{P} when}

##{
 s_W(\pi_0)\leq\alpha,
 \qquad
 \mathbb E[s_W(\Pi_P)]\geq\beta.
}

\p{This is an FTIP proposal motivated by the elicitation-versus-acquisition
debate in \citet{Sections 1 and 4}{liu2025understanding} and
\citet{Sections 1 and 3--4}{yue2025does}. The witness
must specify its threshold, sampling procedure, and independence conditions.
An appealing trace selected after observing the trained model is insufficient.}

\p{The family may encode a strategy class, a transfer set, or another
independently checked event. A witness is finite evidence, not proof of exact
support expansion. It strengthens a gain claim by testing a declared
alternative explanation.}
